# Target paths chezmoi must REMOVE from ~. `apply` only ever writes, so deleting a source file
# leaves its target in place forever; this is the one mechanism that retires one.
#
# Safe to delete an entry once every machine has applied it — the removal is idempotent, so
# there is no cost to leaving one here except the reading. Empty file is fine; delete the file
# when nothing is listed.

# The owned-orgs parser, retired in favour of action-scoped rules (--exclude-tools on the MCP
# registration, gh verb rules in permissions.deny, one rule in CLAUDE.md). Its suite never
# landed in ~ — .chezmoiignore keeps tests/ out — so only these two need removing.
.claude/hooks/repo-scope-guard.sh
.claude/hooks/guard-lib.sh
